This is You


There is a pair of eyes
That always try to catch a glimpse of you,
Always wait for your magnificent smile,
Eagerly longing for eye contact.
It's all the mistake of the eyes and none of mine.

There is a beating heart
That sometimes races,
At times skipping a beat
At the mere sight of you.
It's all the heart's mistake and none of mine.

There is a stable mind
That sometimes becomes unstable—
Sometimes intentionally,
And sometimes unintentionally
It follows you, knowing it's wrong.
It’s all the mind’s mistake, not mine.

All three of them commit the mistakes,
And it's the soul that bears the pain.
I couldn't separate them because
Not only are they a part of me,
But they are me.

In the game of love,
I am only the thief
Who wants to be caught,
But only if you are the detective.